			(property "Description" "High-efficiency synchronous buck converter, adjustable output 0.6V to VIN (600mV typ FB reference, 594-606mV over 0-125C per Table 6.5), 2A rated (TPS62A02 variant), PSM+PWM auto power-save mode for light-load efficiency, PG (Power Good, open-drain, left unconnected/optional here per datasheet Section 5) SOT-23-6 DDC package -- ordering part TPS62A02PDDCR. Real TI datasheet SLUSEG9E (Dec 2021, rev. June 2024), https://www.ti.com/lit/gpn/tps62a02 -- verified directly: Table 5-1 Pin Functions (1=EN,2=GND,3=SW,4=VIN,5=PG,6=FB, SOT23-6 DDC package), Table 6.1 Absolute Maximum Ratings (VIN -0.3 to 6.5V), Table 6.3 Recommended Operating Conditions (VIN 2.5-5.5V), Table 6.5 Electrical Characteristics (VFB 600mV typ, IQ 23uA typ non-switching). Chosen over the higher-current-rail-oriented TPS563201/TPS563200 family (VIN 4.5-17V min -- incompatible with this board's single-cell Li-Ion +VSYS battery-only condition, which can sag to ~3.0V) specifically because TPS62A0x's 2.5-5.5V input range covers both the ~3.0-4.4V Li-Ion-only condition and the ~5V-class wall/USB-present condition documented in power_bms_notes.md, with the 6.5V absolute-max VIN giving margin over MCP73871's own 7.0V IN abs-max. Flattened cache copy of KiCad's real Regulator_Switching:TPS62A02PDDCR (which normally uses (extends \"TPS62A01PDDC\") for its graphics/pins) -- flattened here (graphics/pins duplicated directly, no extends) for the identical kicad-cli headless-loader limitation already documented for AO3401A on power_bms.kicad_sch (see power_bms_notes.md, \"AO3401A extends-symbol issue\"). Pinout (1=EN,2=GND,3=SW,4=VIN,5=PG,6=FB) verified identical to the real TPS62A01PDDC base graphic, which the whole TPS62A0x family shares per the datasheet's own Figure 5-1 SOT23-6 DDC package diagram."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
