	(text "Regulation -- +VSYS to +3V3_SYS buck converter (U8)"
		(at 60 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5926d5cf-017c-4cf8-a16a-c71477f01801")
	)
	(text "Placement only: no wires or global labels on this sheet yet.\nU8 = TPS62A02PDDCR (TI, real datasheet SLUSEG9E), a 2.5-5.5V-in / 2A synchronous\nbuck converter, adjustable output via R8/R9 feedback divider (R8=453k, R9=100k,\nVOUT = 0.6V x (1+R1/R2) = 0.6V x 5.53 = ~3.318V per Eq.2 of the datasheet).\nL1=1uH + C20=4.7uF (VIN) + C21=22uF (VOUT) per the datasheet's own Table 8-3\nrecommended LC combination for VOUT>=1.8V; C22=120pF optional feedforward cap\nacross R8, per the datasheet's own PSM-ripple-reduction note.\nIntended rail names (not yet wired): input = +VSYS (from power_bms.kicad_sch's\nMCP73871 OUT/VBATT_PROT node), output = +3V3_SYS (new regulated rail feeding\nU3 on connectivity.kicad_sch and U4-U7 on uwb_anchors.kicad_sch). EN (pin 1) and\nPG (pin 5, unused/optional) are also left unconnected here -- EN needs to be tied\nto +VSYS (always-on) in a future wiring pass. See regulation_notes.md for the full\ncurrent-budget math and datasheet citations."
		(at 60 38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0d4364a9-4abf-43cb-9b54-758fd777b155")
	)
